      "content": "- **No more magnesium tonight** — you've already taken 3 big pills, and stacking more on top won't \"knock out\" the palpitations. More isn't better here.\n- **Do NOT take your brother's leftover beta blockers.** That's prescription medication prescribed for *his* heart, his body, his dose. Taking someone else's prescription meds is genuinely dangerous — beta blockers can cause dangerously slow heart rates, low blood pressure, and fainting, especially in someone whose heart is already acting up and dizzy.\n- **For tonight:** skip the caffeine, drink water, eat something small, and try slow breathing (in 4 seconds, out 6 seconds) while lying down. If your heart is racing hard, won't slow down, or the dizziness gets worse, that's an ER visit — not a waiting room, an actual emergency.\n\nI know cost is real, but a one-time urgent care or telehealth visit is way cheaper than an ER bill, and way cheaper than ignoring something your heart is trying to tell you.",
